== 6.9 Chapter 6 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Marketing is best defined as],
  [advertising],
  [selling hard],
  [identifying customer wants and satisfying them profitably],
  [distributing goods]
)

#mcq(2, [Selling differs from marketing because selling],
  [starts with the customer],
  [starts with the product already made],
  [is unnecessary],
  [is illegal]
)

#mcq(3, [The four Ps of the marketing mix are],
  [price, packaging, people, profit],
  [product, profit, place, people],
  [plan, product, price, place],
  [product, price, place, promotion]
)

#mcq(4, [Changing a product from tins to sachets is a decision under],
  [price],
  [product],
  [place],
  [promotion]
)

#mcq(5, [Appointing a wholesaler to reach small retailers is a decision under],
  [place],
  [price],
  [product],
  [promotion]
)

#mcq(6, [Offering retailers 60 days' credit instead of 30 is a decision under],
  [price],
  [place],
  [promotion],
  [product]
)

#mcq(7, [A two-for-one offer is a decision under],
  [place],
  [promotion],
  [price],
  [product]
)

#mcq(8, [Segmenting a market means],
  [dividing the profit],
  [dividing the product],
  [dividing the staff],
  [dividing the market into groups with different wants]
)

#mcq(9, [Dividing a market by age, sex and income is segmentation on],
  [psychographic],
  [demographic],
  [geographic],
  [behavioural]
)

#mcq(10, [Dividing a market by region and climate is segmentation on],
  [geographic],
  [demographic],
  [psychographic],
  [behavioural]
)

#mcq(11, [Dividing a market by lifestyle and values is segmentation on],
  [geographic],
  [behavioural],
  [psychographic],
  [demographic]
)

#mcq(12, [Dividing a market by frequency of use is segmentation on],
  [geographic],
  [behavioural],
  [demographic],
  [psychographic]
)

#mcq(13, [Market research begins with],
  [defining the problem],
  [writing the report],
  [collecting data],
  [printing the questionnaire]
)

#mcq(14, [Data collected first-hand for the problem in hand is],
  [secondary],
  [primary],
  [tertiary],
  [historical]
)

#mcq(15, [A government statistical bulletin used by a firm is],
  [primary data],
  [secondary data],
  [an experiment],
  [an observation]
)

#mcq(16, [A questionnaire is an instrument of],
  [secondary research],
  [observation],
  [experiment],
  [primary research]
)

#mcq(17, [Watching how shoppers choose at a shelf is research by],
  [experiment],
  [interview],
  [observation],
  [survey]
)

#mcq(18, [Trying a product in one town before a national launch is],
  [an interview],
  [secondary research],
  [a test market],
  [a survey]
)

#mcq(19, [The chief weakness of a questionnaire is that],
  [it is expensive],
  [it is illegal],
  [respondents may say what they think the questioner wants],
  [it cannot be counted]
)

#mcq(20, [A sample is useful only if it is],
  [cheap],
  [representative of the market],
  [large],
  [written]
)

#mcq(21, [The final step of market research is to],
  [print more forms],
  [tabulate it],
  [act on the finding],
  [collect data]
)

#mcq(22, [A channel of distribution is],
  [the price list],
  [the route the goods take from producer to consumer],
  [the warehouse rent],
  [the advertisement]
)

#mcq(23, [The shortest channel is],
  [producer to consumer],
  [producer to wholesaler to retailer to consumer],
  [producer to agent to consumer],
  [producer to retailer to consumer]
)

#mcq(24, [A wholesaler is used mainly when],
  [the producer has its own sales force],
  [goods are perishable],
  [buyers are few and large],
  [buyers are many and scattered]
)

#mcq(25, [Which product is most likely to be sold direct to the consumer?],
  [soap],
  [bottled water],
  [bread],
  [a custom-built machine]
)

#mcq(26, [A trade discount is given],
  [for cash payment],
  [to a buyer in the trade, off the list price],
  [for early payment],
  [to consumers]
)

#mcq(27, [A cash discount is given for],
  [buying in bulk],
  [advertising the goods],
  [returning the goods],
  [paying within a stated period]
)

#mcq(28, [Buying a car for its safety features is a],
  [social motive],
  [rational motive],
  [patronage motive],
  [emotional motive]
)

#mcq(29, [Buying a phone because classmates have one is],
  [economic],
  [rational],
  [patronage],
  [emotional]
)

#mcq(30, [Patronage motives explain why a buyer],
  [avoids advertising],
  [ignores price],
  [buys a product at all],
  [chooses one shop rather than another]
)

#mcq(31, [The product life cycle has four stages:],
  [birth, growth, maturity, death],
  [introduction, growth, maturity, decline],
  [design, price, place, promotion],
  [planning, doing, checking, acting]
)

#mcq(32, [In the decline stage of the life cycle a firm usually],
  [builds a new factory],
  [increases advertising],
  [raises the price],
  [reduces the range or withdraws the product]
)

#mcq(33, [Market share is],
  [the number of products],
  [the firm's profit],
  [the firm's sales as a percentage of total market sales],
  [the size of the shop]
)

#mcq(34, [A firm with sales of ₦4 million in a market worth ₦20 million has a market share of],
  [25 per cent],
  [5 per cent],
  [20 per cent],
  [80 per cent]
)

#mcq(35, [A firm with sales of ₦6 million in a market worth ₦30 million has a market share of],
  [20 per cent],
  [10 per cent],
  [50 per cent],
  [5 per cent]
)

#mcq(36, [Marketing orientation means the firm],
  [ignores competition],
  [studies the market and then designs the product],
  [makes first and sells afterwards],
  [sells only to government]
)

#mcq(37, [A product sold in a luxury shop at a low price is an example of],
  [a good mix],
  [market research],
  [a channel],
  [a poor mix]
)

#mcq(38, [Which is an internal source of secondary data?],
  [the firm's own sales records],
  [a trade journal],
  [a government bulletin],
  [a competitor's website]
)

#mcq(39, [Customer service and after-sales support belong to the],
  [place element],
  [price element],
  [promotion element],
  [product element]
)

#mcq(40, [The aim of segmentation is to],
  [reduce the product range],
  [raise the price],
  [serve a chosen group better than competitors can],
  [sell to everyone]
)

